# Draw a declarative JSON scene directly with the pen.
#
# The scene format is identical to render_preview: millimetres on the
# scene canvas, origin at the lower-left corner, +X right, +Y up.
#
#   {
#     "width_mm": 180, "height_mm": 150,
#     "strokes": [[[10,10], [20,20], [30,10]]],
#     "shapes": [{"type": "circle", "cx": 90, "cy": 75, "r": 30}]
#   }
#
# Supported shapes: line, polyline/path, polygon, rect, circle, ellipse,
# arc. Each stroke/shape may set width_mm and closed; width is ignored for
# plotting because the pen tip defines the line width. Fills, colours and
# text are not supported (text lives in the separate text skill).
#
# Unlike render_preview followed by image, this tool never rasterises
# the scene and never traces ink outlines. Every stroke becomes exactly one
# pen-down polyline, so a line is drawn once instead of as two parallel
# outline sides, and circles/arcs keep the geometry that was requested.
# Use scene for actual plotting; use render_preview (only enabled
# when config debug=true) when a PNG preview or a file for another tool
# is needed.
#
# The canvas origin is placed at the workspace origin plus offset_x/
# offset_y (millimetres). width_mm/height_mm default to the skill config
# and must fit the workspace. The whole scene is validated before the
# machine moves: any point outside the workspace, an empty scene, or more
# than the configured max_points rejects the request and no motion is sent.
#
# dry_run=true plans and returns the counts/bounding box without moving.
#
# Before the trajectory, the primitive HOME routine runs unless skip_home
# is true (use it when the pilot already called plotter_home). After a
# successful draw, auto_home runs the HOME routine again.
#
# When debug=true, this tool also writes a preview PNG to
# output_dir/last_preview.png before moving, unless skip_preview is true
# (use it when the pilot already called render_preview). A preview failure
# is reported as a warning and never blocks drawing.
#
# The global motion profile (velocity/acceleration/deceleration/jerk) and
# pen heights are owned by the plotter primitive: change them with
# plotter_set_params. This tool never calls SET_PARAM.
string  spec
# Millimetres added to the scene origin inside the workspace.
float64 offset_x
float64 offset_y
# Plan only: return point count, do not move the machine.
bool    dry_run
# Run the primitive HOME routine after a successful draw.
bool    auto_home
# The pilot already homed before this call; do not repeat HOME.
bool    skip_home
# The pilot already wrote the preview; do not render it again.
bool    skip_preview
plot/Workspace workspace
---
bool    success
string  message
# Pen-up/down waypoints sent to the primitive.
uint32  points
# Strokes/shapes in the scene after shape expansion.
uint32  strokes
float64 width_mm
float64 height_mm
float64 min_x
float64 max_x
float64 min_y
float64 max_y
float64 elapsed_s